<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/">
	<!--
		Embedded libraries, in dependency order.

		WhatTheWhisper ships its own copies so that unzipping the addon folder is
		the whole installation: there is no "## Dependencies: Ace3" and nothing
		else to download. The files under here are byte-for-byte upstream Ace3 and
		are never patched -- another addon may end up using whichever copy loads
		first, so a local change here would silently become their code too.
		Anything WhatTheWhisper-specific lives in Core/ instead.

		Sharing is the point, not a hazard: every file below registers through
		LibStub's MAJOR/MINOR mechanism, so if another addon already loaded a
		newer revision of a library, that one keeps its place and ours is skipped;
		if ours is newer, it upgrades theirs in place and existing consumers keep
		working. That is why the order below matters and why nothing here is
		namespaced.

		Order:
		  1. LibStub            -- the registry everything else registers with
		  2. CallbackHandler    -- needed by AceEvent and AceDB
		  3. AceAddon           -- the addon object; no further dependencies
		  4. AceConsole         -- slash commands; LibStub only
		  5. AceEvent           -- needs CallbackHandler
		  6. AceDB              -- needs CallbackHandler
		  7. AceLocale          -- LibStub only

		Only these seven are embedded, because only these seven are used.
		LibSharedMedia-3.0 is deliberately absent: it is queried with
		LibStub("LibSharedMedia-3.0", true) and used only if some other addon
		provides it, so embedding it would add weight for an integration that is
		optional by design.
	-->
	<Script file="LibStub\LibStub.lua"/>
	<Include file="CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.xml"/>
	<Include file="AceAddon-3.0\AceAddon-3.0.xml"/>
	<Include file="AceConsole-3.0\AceConsole-3.0.xml"/>
	<Include file="AceEvent-3.0\AceEvent-3.0.xml"/>
	<Include file="AceDB-3.0\AceDB-3.0.xml"/>
	<Include file="AceLocale-3.0\AceLocale-3.0.xml"/>
</Ui>
